        "original_id": "bdc58648-6aa5-5021-a6f1-8ebe9d40906a",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: André Previn, Edie Landau, Eugene O'Neill, Boris Kaufman\n- Works: Long Day's Journey into Night (1962 film), O'Neill's play\n- Roles: composer, pianist, conductor, cinematographer, producer, executive\n- Projects: The American Film Theatre\n\nFacts:\n- André Previn was born Andreas Ludwig Priwin on April 6, 1929, and he is a German-American pianist, conductor, and composer.\n- Edie Landau was born Edythe Rudolph on July 15, 1927, and she is an American film and TV producer and executive.\n- The 1962 film Long Day's Journey into Night used Eugene O'Neill's play directly rather than adapting the screenplay.\n- The 1962 film Long Day's Journey into Night had a music score by André Previn and cinematography by Boris Kaufman.\n- Edie Landau is known for films including Long Day's Journey into Night, The Pawnbroker, and The Chosen.\n- Edie Landau produced the fourteen movies of The American Film Theatre with her husband Ely A. Landau.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
